{"content":[{"c":["MORTAR*, The"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Name given by Zephaniah to a hollow place or depression resembling a mortar in Jerusalem. The “mortar” (Hebrew, ",{"c":["Maktesh"],"sourceClass":"hebrew","t":"span"},") was a place of business whose merchants were soon to grieve for their loss of trade (",{"href":"?bref=Zeph.1.11","r":"Zeph.1.11","rawR":"Zeph.1.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Zeph.1.11","value":"Zeph.1.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Zep 1:11"},"). Its location is variously identified with the Phoenician quarter, the Kidron Valley, or the Tyropoeon Valley."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Jerusalem_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Jerusalem_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Jerusalem_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Jerusalem"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Mortarthe","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Zep 1:11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Zeph.1.11","rawQueryValue":"Zeph.1.11","sourceRefExact":"Zeph.1.11"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"80a6caad30b8702f4b34c92b62392a5055246ca8f2932de226f4f49cef912a4d","sourceItemName":"Mortarthe","sourceItemOrder":402,"sourceMember":"Articles/M.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Mortarthe","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Mortar*, the","title":"Mortar*, the","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}